From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luciano Dittgen <luciano.dittgen@ossystems.com.br>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:31:12 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] zram-init: Pass the device number to hot_remove

The zram-control hot_remove attribute takes the device id ("0"), not
the device node path. Writing "/dev/zram0" fails with EINVAL, so
"zram-init 0" reports "failed to reset zram0" and exits 1 even though
the swap was turned off and the device reset. Under systemd this makes
ExecStop of zram_swap.service fail.

Write $dev instead of $devnode.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Luciano Dittgen <luciano.dittgen@ossystems.com.br>
---
 sbin/zram-init.in | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sbin/zram-init.in b/sbin/zram-init.in
index f577cfc..56d9108 100755
--- a/sbin/zram-init.in
+++ b/sbin/zram-init.in
@@ -346,7 +346,7 @@ then	if $swap
 		then	zramctl --reset -- "$devnode" || status=$?
 		else	SysCtl 1 "$block/reset" || status=$?
 			if $umount && test -w "$zclass/hot_remove"
-			then	SysCtl "$devnode" "$zclass/hot_remove" \
+			then	SysCtl "$dev" "$zclass/hot_remove" \
 					|| status=$?
 			fi
 		fi
